      "text": "Step 1: Understand the problem and the given information.\n- The pressure of a gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature.\n- We have an oxygen sample in a 2.28 liter container with a pressure of 5 kPa.\n- We need to find the new pressure when the oxygen is moved to a 5.7 liter container at the same temperature.\n\nStep 2: Apply the inverse proportionality concept.\n- According to the inverse proportionality, when two quantities are inversely proportional, their product is constant.\n- Let P1 be the initial pressure, V1 be the initial volume, P2 be the new pressure, and V2 be the new volume.\n- The relationship can be expressed as P1 * V1 = P2 * V2.\n\nStep 3: Set up the equation with the given values.\n- P1 = 5 kPa\n- V1 = 2.28 liters\n- V2 = 5.7 liters\n\n- Substitute the values into the equation: 5 * 2.28 = P2 * 5.7.\n\nStep 4: Solve for P2.\n- 11.4 = P2 * 5.7\n- Divide both sides by 5.7 to isolate P2: P2 = 11.4 / 5.7\n- P2 = 2 kPa\n\nAnswer: The new pressure in the 5.7 liter container, at the same temperature, will be \\boxed{2} kPa.",
