      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula that relates pressure (P) and volume (V) at constant temperature: \\(P1V1 = P2V2\\), where \\(P1\\) and \\(V1\\) are the initial pressure and volume, and \\(P2\\) and \\(V2\\) are the final pressure and volume.\n\nGiven:\n- \\(P1 = 5 \\text{ kPa}\\)\n- \\(V1 = 2.28 \\text{ liters}\\)\n- \\(V2 = 5.7 \\text{ liters}\\)\n\nWe need to find \\(P2\\).\n\nUsing the formula \\(P1V1 = P2V2\\), we can solve for \\(P2\\):\n\n\\[\nP2 = \\frac{P1V1}{V2}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\nP2 = \\frac{5 \\text{ kPa} \\times 2.28 \\text{ liters}}{5.7 \\text{ liters}}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nP1 = 5  # kPa\nV1 = 2.28  # liters\nV2 = 5.7  # liters\n\n# Calculate the final pressure P2\nP2 = (P1 * V1) / V2\nprint(P2)\n```\n```output\n2.0\n```\nThe new pressure inside the 5.7-liter container at the same temperature will be \\(\\boxed{2.0}\\) kPa.",
