      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the relationship between pressure and volume for a gas at constant temperature, which is given by Boyle's Law. Boyle's Law states that the pressure of a given mass of gas is inversely proportional to its volume. Mathematically, this can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ P_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2 \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( P_1 \\) is the initial pressure,\n- \\( V_1 \\) is the initial volume,\n- \\( P_2 \\) is the final pressure,\n- \\( V_2 \\) is the final volume.\n\nWe are given:\n- \\( P_1 = 5 \\) kPa,\n- \\( V_1 = 2.28 \\) liters,\n- \\( V_2 = 5.7 \\) liters.\n\nWe need to find \\( P_2 \\). Rearranging Boyle's Law to solve for \\( P_2 \\):\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{V_2} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values into the equation:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\]\n\nNow, let's perform the multiplication and division:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{11.4 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\]\n\\[ P_2 = 2 \\, \\text{kPa} \\]\n\nTherefore, the new pressure when moving all of the oxygen to a 5.7 liter container at the same temperature is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) kPa.",
